<Base title="How App Composer works" description="Understand the supported agent-operated workflow, independent app contracts, ownership, configuration, updates and safe rollback."><h1>You direct.<br/>Your agent delivers.</h1><p class="lede">App Composer prepares a real environment and joins independently maintained apps. It uses external Codex for execution and EmDash for its managed catalogue; it does not host a competing agent.</p><section class="section"><h2>From no idea to a live app</h2><ol><li><strong>Get Ready.</strong> The agent checks its actual workspace, GitHub and Cloudflare tools. It verifies the target and deploys the configurable Hello World reference over HTTPS.</li><li><strong>Init.</strong> Choose a useful preset and customise real fields. Export a versioned spec and a matching prompt, without credentials.</li><li><strong>Compose.</strong> Pin independent source commits, validate their declared routes, data versions and capabilities, and connect their real item/action interface.</li><li><strong>Verify.</strong> Check source identity and live interaction, not just HTTP 200 or a green build.</li></ol></section><section class="section"><h2>The first composition</h2><p>Photo Guestbook owns submitted media, moderation and eligibility. Curated Showcase owns its card collection. An approved item can be selected and featured; opening its card opens the source contribution. Unavailable, hidden or deleted sources fail closed. Composer joins the routes through Worker service bindings; there are no iframes or private media copies.</p><p><a href="/catalogue">Browse the EmDash catalogue</a> · <a href="/demo">Use the live pair</a></p></section><section class="section"><h2>Updates preserve your work.</h2><p>App configuration and owner data live separately from upstream source. A candidate must keep the supported contract and data version, pass capability checks and use exact commits. Incompatible versions or new permissions are rejected before activation. Your working release stays live.</p><p>The first path uses explicit, validated promotion through repository commands. Automatic branch following and webhook-driven updates remain unshipped until their concurrency and conflict gates are proven.</p><p>Code rollback restores an executable only. It never restores an old database, republishes a hidden image or discards later submissions. Storage exports and backups have their own authorised recovery path.</p></section><section class="section"><h2>The supported boundary</h2><p>This first release is operated by an authorised agent using its own GitHub/Cloudflare runtime. Public users can browse examples, explore decisions and export a spec. They cannot launch arbitrary builds, access production credentials or moderate another owner’s collection.</p><p>Owner uploads are capped and invited. No current feature implies a public multi-tenant security guarantee, provider partnership or commercial agreement.</p><p><a href="/state">Try fictional encrypted assistant state</a> · <a href="/extension">Optional Cloudflare dashboard extension</a> · <a href="/release">Verified release evidence</a></p></section></Base>
